---
import Layout from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Papers are listed newest-first. Each renders as its own embedded-viewer
// section. Generic filenames keep program identifiers out of URLs.
const papers = [
  {
    id: 'campaign-retrieval-optimization',
    featured: true,
    title: 'Campaign Retrieval Optimization',
    subtitle:
      'A large-neighborhood search over retrieval campaigns: its architecture, and what it can and cannot save',
    pdf: '/campaign-retrieval-optimization-white-paper.pdf',
    pages: 22,
    date: 'October 2026 · Rev. 0',
    abstract:
      'This paper documents a new optimization layer over the campaign retrieval model: a large-neighborhood search that keeps the baseline campaign set, repeatedly destroys and rebuilds small groups of campaigns under all of the same sequencing and waste acceptance rules, and accepts a rebuilt set only when the exact glass formulation model confirms the mission needs less glass. The central finding is a negative result worth knowing: inverse waste loading is nearly linear in blend composition, so total mission glass is almost independent of how waste is partitioned into campaigns. What the search actually buys is structure: across all 32 published mission scenarios it cut campaign count by 20.0% (2,284 to 1,827) while trimming glass by 0.057%, with 17 scenarios improving on canisters and none worsening.',
    highlights: [
      'Large-neighborhood search with verification-gated, strictly-improving acceptance',
      'Exact glass-formulation evaluation of every candidate mission (multi-start SLSQP)',
      'The linearity result: inverse waste loading fits blend composition at R² = 0.79, explaining why greedy repartitioning loses',
      'Suite-wide: -20.0% campaigns, -216 canisters, 0 scenarios worsened across 32 published scenarios',
      'Reference case: a 16-campaign chain of capped campaigns collapsed to 5 by cross-blending layers the baseline kept apart',
      'Every result passed the full hard-rule battery: precedence, volume bands, mass conservation, WAC compliance',
      'Blend-signature memoization: 116,895 cache hits to 3,970 exact solves (29.4:1)',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'mission-modeling',
    featured: false,
    title: 'Coupled Mission Planning and Facility Process Modeling',
    subtitle: 'Architecture and algorithms of the campaign builder and the facility process model',
    pdf: '/mission-modeling-white-paper.pdf',
    pages: 28,
    date: 'October 2026',
    abstract:
      'This paper documents two coupled applications that model the end-to-end mission from published tank inventory chemistry through sequenced retrieval campaigns to glass. The campaign builder turns per-tank data into feed blends with WAC evaluation and glass-forming optimization; the facility model simulates the melter, off-gas treatment train, condensate chemistry, and the operator schedule, with mass and energy closure enforced throughout and verified against published benchmarks.',
    highlights: [
      'End-to-end lineage from published inventory data to stack composition and operator schedules',
      'Campaign generation under published sequencing rules with linear-program blend optimization',
      'Glass formulation as constrained nonlinear optimization (SLSQP with multi-start)',
      'Element-conserving melter partition engine with residual-ledger verification',
      'Full off-gas train: scrubber, WESP, HEME, HEPA, adsorber beds, RHX/SCO/SCR',
      'Wash-efficiency sensitivity study: retrieval strategy nearly doubles mission glass',
      'Verification: 147 automated tests, per-species closure, energy closure, boundary audits',
    ],
  },
];

const dashboard = {
  title: 'Interactive dashboard',
  cta: 'Demo access available on request',
  features: [
    {
      title: 'Process flow diagram',
      detail:
        'A live PFD redrawn from model state each campaign: unit boxes with key properties (melter duty, scrubber quench, bed loadings), stream arrows carrying real T/P/flow, and side-product stubs for glass and effluent.',
      shot: '/assets/dash-shot-1.png',
      shotCaption:
        'Live PFD of the melter and off-gas train for the selected campaign, with per-unit properties and stream labels driven by the model state.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Mission trends',
      detail:
        'Cached mission sweeps rendered as interactive trends: campaign runtimes, glass mass, canister counts, and off-gas loadings across the full schedule, with per-campaign drill-down.',
      shot: '/assets/dash-shot-2.png',
      shotCaption:
        'Glass composition and cumulative glass/canister output trends across the mission schedule from the Trends view.',
    },
    {
      title: 'Streams & ledgers',
      detail:
        'Every computed stream exposed as composition tables: speciated feed, melter products, each off-gas stage, condensate chemistry. Element ledgers close per species and per unit.',
      shot: '/assets/dash-shot-4.png',
      shotCaption:
        'Speciated stream composition for the melter off-gas stream, with phase, molar flow, mol-fraction, and mass flow per species.',
    },
  ],
};

// Fourth screenshot kept for the blog post / future use
const extraShots = [
  {
    shot: '/assets/dash-shot-3.png',
    note:
      'Effluent quantity & composition trends across mission days (from the Effluent tab).',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="White papers & dashboard"
  description="Two mission-modeling white papers (campaign retrieval optimization and coupled mission planning) and the interactive Streamlit dashboard built on the facility mission model."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Deliverables</p>
      <h1>White papers & dashboard</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The full write-ups of the mission-modeling toolchain, and the interactive
        dashboard that sits on top of it. Read each paper inline below; explore the
        dashboard's capabilities after.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- Papers: summaries only, PDF on request ---------- -->
  {
    papers.map((paper) => (
      <section class="section-sm paper-section" id={paper.id}>
        <div class="container">
          {paper.featured && <p class="eyebrow new-flag">New</p>}
          <div class="paper-grid">
            <div class="paper-info glass-card">
              <span class="badge">
                {paper.pages} pages · {paper.date}
              </span>
              <h2>{paper.title}</h2>
              <p class="paper-subtitle">{paper.subtitle}</p>
              <p class="paper-abstract">{paper.abstract}</p>

              <div class="paper-highlights">
                <h3>What's in it</h3>
                <ul>
                  {paper.highlights.map((highlight) => (
                    <li>{highlight}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="paper-access glass-card">
              <div class="paper-access-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M6 2h8l5 5v13a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2Z" />
                  <path d="M14 2v6h6" />
                  <path d="M16 13H8" />
                  <path d="M16 17H8" />
                  <path d="M10 9H8" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Full paper available on request</h3>
              <p>
                The complete {paper.pages}-page write-up, with full methodology, results
                tables, and verification evidence, is available for reading on request.
              </p>
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Request a copy</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </section>
    ))
  }

  <!-- ---------- Dashboard feature ---------- -->
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Tooling</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">{dashboard.title}</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Built on the facility mission model, a Streamlit application gives process and
        mission-planning engineers a real-time view of the whole train: campaign inputs,
        unit-by-unit streams, energy and effluent ledgers, and the discrete operator
        schedule, all interactive.
      </p>

      <div class="card-grid cols-3 dash-grid">
        {
          dashboard.features.map((feature) => (
            <div class="glass-card dash-card">
              <figure class="shot-frame">
                <img
                  src={feature.shot}
                  alt={feature.shotCaption}
                  loading="lazy"
                />
                <figcaption>{feature.shotCaption}</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <h3>{feature.title}</h3>
              <p>{feature.detail}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="glass-card dash-cta">
        <div>
          <h3>See it live</h3>
          <p>
            The dashboard runs against the full dataset and isn't public-facing, but I'm
            happy to walk through it: PFD, trends, streams, exports, and the discrete
            operations schedule.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">{dashboard.cta}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ---------- Papers ---------- */
  .new-flag {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .paper-section {
    scroll-margin-top: 5.5rem;
  }

  .paper-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .paper-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 3fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .paper-info {
    padding: 1.75rem 1.9rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .paper-info:hover {
    transform: none;
  }

  .paper-info h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  .paper-subtitle {
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .paper-abstract {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .paper-highlights h3 {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .paper-highlights ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }

  .paper-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  .paper-access {
    padding: 1.75rem 1.9rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .paper-access:hover {
    transform: none;
  }

  .paper-access-icon {
    width: 3.5rem;
    height: 3.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-glow);
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
  }

  .paper-access-icon svg {
    width: 1.8rem;
    height: 1.8rem;
  }

  .paper-access h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .paper-access p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  @media print {
    .paper-access {
      border: none;
      box-shadow: none;
    }
    .paper-access .btn {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- Dashboard ---------- */
  .section-title {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .dash-grid {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .dash-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .dash-card:hover {
    transform: none;
  }

  .dash-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .dash-card p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .shot-frame {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .shot-frame img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--surface-solid);
  }

  .shot-frame figcaption {
    padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .shot-shot {
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--gradient-soft);
    min-height: 9.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .shot-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    background: var(--gradient);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
  }

  .shot-sub {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .dash-cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .dash-cta:hover {
    transform: none;
  }

  .dash-cta h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .dash-cta p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
</style>
